/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A symmetric planar guide is a core layer of index n₁ and thickness d between two claddings of index n₂, with n₁ > n₂.
   - In each layer Maxwell's equations reduce to the wave equation.
   - k₀ = 2π/λ is the free-space wavenumber (λ the vacuum wavelength) and n is n₁ in the core and n₂ in the cladding.
   - At x = ±d/2 the tangential components of E and H must be continuous.
   - These equations have only a few roots, so only a few values of β are allowed.
   - Two families exist.
   - The mode number m counts the zeros of the field across the core.
   - One number collects thickness, wavelength and index step:
   - V is the normalized frequency (dimensionless); d is the full core thickness; λ is the vacuum wavelength in the same unit as d; √(n₁² − n₂²) is the NA of the index step.
   - With this V, mode m is guided when V > mπ, so a symmetric guide carries floor(V/π) + 1 modes of each family, and it is single-mode when V < π.
*/
